# Prettier's scope is this package's sources under src/ — that is what
# `pnpm format:check` checks and what the pre-commit hook formats.
#
# The four-line allowlist chain that used to stand here is gone with the move:
# Prettier's root is this directory now, so an unscoped `prettier --write .`
# cannot reach outside the package at all. What the chain was defending against
# is worth remembering, because it was not hypothetical — an unscoped run has
# re-expanded the minified docs/assets/logo.svg into a 300-line diff and reached
# the vendored conformance vectors under tests/, which must never be edited.
# Those all live above this directory now.
#
# What remains is the one exclusion that is genuinely INSIDE the package:
# generated snapshots are not sources and Prettier must not rewrite them.
src/**/*.snap
